  "kind": "quirk",
  "title": "Under a single-byte Windows locale such as en-ZA, the B-suffixed text functions count characters rather than UTF-8 or UTF-16 bytes",
  "statement": "In Excel 16.0.20527.20088 with user culture en-ZA (a single-byte Windows code page), LENB, LEFTB, RIGHTB, MIDB, FINDB, SEARCHB, and REPLACEB count characters rather than UTF-8 or UTF-16 bytes: LENB(UNICHAR(20013)) returns 1, LEFTB(UNICHAR(20013)&\"abc\",2) returns \"中a\", and FINDB(\"b\",UNICHAR(20013)&\"b\") returns 2 (double-byte counting applies only under DBCS languages such as ja-JP, ko-KR, or zh-CN).",
  "status": "measured",
  "basis": "Measured across rows 18-27 of dczsn3_bytes in Excel 16.0.20527.20088 (en-ZA) and matched across full-bank rows (LENB 2,083/2,083, LEFTB 2,478/2,478, RIGHTB 2,481/2,481, MIDB 2,913/2,913, FINDB 2,861/2,861, SEARCHB 2,861/2,861, REPLACEB 2,951/2,951).",
